0.1.3 (2026-11-04)
  * Off by default; the retired auto value means off. Keep explicit yes and amd-dgpu choices.
  * Read registered regions immediately with no polling in any mode; diagnose only an opt-in that cannot work.
  * Name drm and NVIDIA regions, including NVIDIA eight-digit PCI domains.
  * The Graphics page offers the opt-in through this package's setting.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.2 (2026-11-04)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Keep what cannot work where it should with sparky-stereo-problems (ORDER 346f-1): a SPARKY_STEREO_VRAM_BOOST
    that is not a mode, a kernel without the dmem controller on a computer whose GPU (amdgpu, xe, nouveau) could use
    it, a dmem.capacity that cannot be read, a bound GPU that registered no VRAM; cleared at the boot that finds the
    cause gone. By design, and not problems: mode no, no GPU, and GPUs whose driver registers no VRAM (NVIDIA's own).
  * The messages in the nine languages, as journal catalogs; Depends on sparky-stereo-problems (>= 0.1.2)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.1 (2026-10-25)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * on by default for every GPU that registers its VRAM, Daniel 2026-10-25
  * Keep the old AMD dedicated VRAM rule as SPARKY_STEREO_VRAM_BOOST=amd-dgpu

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2026-10-25)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * Decide at every boot whether dmemcg-booster and plasma-foreground-booster run
  * On by default with an AMD GPU that has its own VRAM and a kernel with the dmem controller
  * SPARKY_STEREO_VRAM_BOOST=auto, yes or no in /etc/default/sparky-stereo-vram-boost
